    "message": {
     "content": "### The Bottom Line: **Yes, you should accept this offer.**\n\nGoogle addressed your exact leverage point: they fully made you whole on your unvested $200,000 in cash upfront, matched your base salary, and left the $1.08M equity intact. \n\nFor an L6 Product Manager in the Bay Area, this is now a top-tier, 90th+ percentile package.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers: Year-by-Year Breakdown\n\nAssuming Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting schedule (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**):\n\n| Year | Base Salary | Target Bonus (20%) | Initial RSU Vest | Sign-On Bonus | Projected Refreshes (Stacking) | **Total Estimated TC** | **Meta Baseline** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $356,400 (33%) | $200,000 | $0 | **~$844,400** | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 2** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $356,400 (33%) | $0 | ~$62,500 | **~$706,900** | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 3** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $237,600 (22%) | $0 | ~$125,000 | **~$650,600** | ~$526,000 |\n| **Year 4** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $129,600 (12%) | $0 | ~$187,500 | **~$605,100** | ~$526,000 |\n\n*(Even if Google uses a flat 25%/year vesting schedule, Year 1 is **~$758,000** and Year 2 is **~$620,500**).*\n\n#### 4-Year Cumulative Advantage\n* **Meta (Status Quo):** ~$2.10M \u2013 $2.20M over 4 years.\n* **Google (Revised Offer):** **~$2.80M+ over 4 years** (a net gain of **~$600,000 to $700,000**).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This Is a Major Win\n\n1. **Guaranteed Cash vs. Paper Risk:** Instead of waiting 12 months for $200,000 of Meta equity to vest (subject to stock volatility), you receive $200,000 in immediate cash, while simultaneously starting the clock on a fresh $1.08M Google equity grant.\n2. **Huge Front-Loaded Earnings:** You will earn **~$1.55M in your first 24 months** at Google. \n3. **No Further Negotiation Upside:** When Google adds a $200k sign-on bonus and explicitly states \"this is our best offer,\" it generally means compensation committee approval was maxed out for that level. Pushing further risks souring the relationship or having the offer rescinded.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Checklist Before Signing\n\nBefore you officially sign the written offer letter, double-check these two administrative details with your recruiter:\n\n* **Sign-On Payment Terms & Clawback:** Confirm that the $200,000 is paid out in your first 1\u20132 paychecks. Verify the clawback period (typically 12 months prorated, meaning you keep 100% of it once you complete Year 1).\n* **Vesting Schedule:** Confirm in writing whether your $1.08M RSU grant follows the front-loaded schedule (33/33/22/12) or equal quarterly distribution (25% per year).",
